  "slug": "functions-augmenting-0a1b",
  "summary": "New code releases and validation tests cover HOD fitting, void finding, N-body convergence and differentiable SPHEREx photometry ahead of Stage IV surveys.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a methodological focus on the infrastructure connecting dark matter structure to survey observables. SciPIC-lite provides a public, flexible Halo Occupation Distribution pipeline for clustering observables. PhotoNs-3 is tested against GADGET for accuracy and convergence in power spectra, halo profiles and mass functions at Stage IV requirements, bearing on the simulated dark matter backbone onto which galaxies are painted. The Popcorn Void Finder reimplementation documents the algorithm and reports a change from a power-law to a Schechter-like void size function. Hesperos and Eosphoros add a differentiable forced-photometry operator and forward model for SPHEREx spectrophotometry. The new element is emphasis on reproducibility, validation and differentiability rather than new astrophysical results; the items address different stages of the pipeline and are not a single analysis chain.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
